From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: mmc: sunxi: the eMMC host starts a read block only when the FIFO has room for it

At HS200 and HS400 the eMMC host now uses the card read threshold
(THLD 0x100: bit 0 on, bits 27:16 = block size) for reads, as the SDIO
host already does for its fast timings. Without it the controller holds
the card clock as soon as its 1 KiB FIFO is full - which can happen in
the middle of a block when the DMA falls behind.

Measured on the HY310 before this patch (arbeit/medien/VE-stabil, part 3,
15.10.2026, with the diagnostic patch 0311, which is not part of this
series, and 0312):

 - data CRC errors on eMMC reads come only while Kodi plays 4K video
   (VE decoding, the GPU taking the frames, cage, display): 22-24 per
   100 MiB for Kodi's own reads, 0.3-28.8 for a dd reader next to it;
 - the same reader saw none in over 40 GB without that load, under CPU
   memory load at 70 degrees C, next to the VE alone and next to the GPU
   at 600 MHz;
 - under the Kodi 4K load the FIFO was full in 2.9 % of 1.26 million
   samples of STAS, without it never; most errors came with the FIFO at
   190 or more of its 256 words;
 - runtime PM made no difference (autosuspend against power/control=on).

Measured with this patch (part 4, 15.10.2026), nine Kodi 4K runs of the
same arms and load (four with Kodi cold, five from its cache with a dd
reader next to it):

 - 30946 MiB read, no data CRC error at all, against 1899 on 19049 MiB in
   nine runs without the threshold;
 - the FIFO was full in 0.001 to 0.002 % of the samples instead of 2.9 %
   (THLD reads 0x02000001 during reads);
 - the dd reader next to Kodi got 133 to 137 MB/s instead of 45 to 128,
   and 152 MB/s without any load, as before;
 - h264 and hevc 1080p decode bit-exact from files read through the eMMC
   (300 of 300 frames each), and a 128 MiB write reads back with the same
   md5.

0312 stays as the net for an error that still comes.
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1780,6 +1780,42 @@
 	writel(rval, host->reg_base + SDXC_REG_THLD);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The eMMC host (not v5p3x) at HS200/HS400: start a block of a read only
+ * when the FIFO has room for all of it. Without the card read threshold
+ * the controller holds the card clock as soon as the FIFO is full, which
+ * can be in the middle of a block. Measured on the HY310 (VE-stabil,
+ * 15.10.2026): while Kodi plays 4K video the DMA falls behind, the FIFO is
+ * full in 2.9 % of the samples (never without that load), and reads see
+ * data CRC errors only under that load, mostly with the FIFO nearly full -
+ * 19 to 742 a minute, against none in over 40 GB without it. With the
+ * threshold the same load read 30946 MiB without a single one, and the
+ * FIFO was full in 0.002 % of the samples instead of 2.9 %.
+ *
+ * Same register layout as the SDIO host above (THLD 0x100: bit 0 read
+ * threshold on, bits 27:16 the threshold in bytes); the threshold is the
+ * block size, 512 bytes, which fits twice into the 1 KiB FIFO. Writes and
+ * the slower timings leave it off, as before.
+ */
+static void sunxi_mmc_thld_ctl_emmc(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host,
+				    struct mmc_data *data)
+{
+	unsigned char timing = host->mmc->ios.timing;
+	u32 rval;
+
+	if (host->cfg->v5p3x || !host->cfg->supports_hs400)
+		return;
+
+	rval = readl(host->reg_base + SDXC_REG_THLD);
+	rval &= ~(SDXC_THLD_SIZE_MASK | SDXC_THLD_READ_EN);
+
+	if ((data->flags & MMC_DATA_READ) && data->blksz <= 512 &&
+	    (timing == MMC_TIMING_MMC_HS200 || timing == MMC_TIMING_MMC_HS400))
+		rval |= (data->blksz << 16) | SDXC_THLD_READ_EN;
+
+	writel(rval, host->reg_base + SDXC_REG_THLD);
+}
+
 static void sunxi_mmc_request(struct mmc_host *mmc, struct mmc_request *mrq)
 {
 	struct sunxi_mmc_host *host = mmc_priv(mmc);
@@ -1888,6 +1924,7 @@
 
 	if (data) {
 		sunxi_mmc_thld_ctl_v5p3x(host, data);
+		sunxi_mmc_thld_ctl_emmc(host, data);
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_BLKSZ, data->blksz);
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_BCNTR, data->blksz * data->blocks);
 		sunxi_mmc_start_dma(host, data);
